\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces A rhombic strip of $\mathcal  B_4$ with some colorfully marked rhombi. The maximal chains represent permutations, and a flip across a rhombus represents an adjacent transposition. The left boundary represents 1234. Flipping across the green rhombus, we obtain 2134. Then, flipping orange, blue, red and finally purple, we obtain 2314, 3214, 3124 and finally 3142. This rhombic strip represents a facet-Hamiltonian path of the 3 dimensional permutahedron. The facet-Hamiltonian path is depicted in \Cref  {fig:perm as truncation}.}}{11}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rhombic to fh example}{{11}{11}{A rhombic strip of $\mathcal B_4$ with some colorfully marked rhombi. The maximal chains represent permutations, and a flip across a rhombus represents an adjacent transposition. The left boundary represents 1234. Flipping across the green rhombus, we obtain 2134. Then, flipping orange, blue, red and finally purple, we obtain 2314, 3214, 3124 and finally 3142. This rhombic strip represents a facet-Hamiltonian path of the 3 dimensional permutahedron. The facet-Hamiltonian path is depicted in \Cref {fig:perm as truncation}}{figure.caption.11}{}}
